---
description: Python typing, docstrings, imports, and class member standards
globs: **/*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

When editing or generating Python:

- Place imports at the top of the file.
- Define class member variables on the class with type annotations before `__init__`.
- Add type annotations to all function parameters, return types, and variables where practical.
- Give each non-trivial function (not one-line trivial wrappers) a PEP 257 docstring with a one-line summary of its purpose; extend it only when behavior, arguments, or return value are non-obvious.

Example:

```python
class VolumeLoader:
    _index: int

    def __init__(self, index: int) -> None:
        self._index = index

    def load_volume(self, url: str) -> Volume:
        """Load a volume descriptor from the given URL."""
```
